# Fixed defect 131, 2026-09-28, beside it: `for` over what is not an
# iteration. Symptom: `for x of xs` over an indented body cost
# `for_missing_in`, whose repair is `while`, and then `missing_body` at `of`,
# and the body the comment above `for_stmt` promises is "still checked" was
# dropped with its mistakes. Cause: the rest of the head, parsed as the
# condition it most likely was, stopped at `of`, and the check for a body
# asked that token. A head that refused something drops the rest of its line
# and reads the body below it (`parse/opening`).

function over_of(xs: [i64])
    for x of xs  #~ for_missing_in
        y = 3 )  #~ expected_end_of_line
    z = 4 )  #~ expected_end_of_line

function main()
    print(1)
